+## Behaviours generated by the `generic-parallel` interface
+
+The `integrate_debug` functions are not available for a behaviour
+generated by the `generic-parallel` interface of `MFront`: they throw an
+exception. Such a behaviour integrates all the points of a batch in one
+call, and only reports the index of the first point where the
+integration failed (member `n` of the `BehaviourIntegrationResult`
+structure, see [this page](generic-parallel.html)).
+
+The same `MFront` file, compiled with the `generic` interface, gives the
+detailed diagnostic at this point: a material data manager of this
+behaviour, on the host, is given the data of the point, and the point is
+integrated by the `integrate_debug` function taking a range of points.
+
 ## Description of the default analyser {#sec:mgis:integration_failure:default_analyser}
 
