+# Support of the `generic-parallel` interface of `MFront`
+
+The behaviours, models and material properties generated by the
+`generic-parallel` interface of `MFront` process whole batches of points,
+on CPUs or on GPUs (`CUDA`, `HIP`, parallel algorithms of the `C++`
+standard library, `Kokkos`, `SYCL`, `OpenMP`). Their support is described
+in a dedicated [page](generic-parallel.html). This support requires a
+version of `TFEL` providing those interfaces (version 2 of the data
+structures of the behaviours and of the functions of the material
+properties). In short:
+
+- the libraries are recognized when they are loaded, and their version,
+  backend and memory space are checked;
+- the existing functions acting on a material data manager
+  (`integrate`, `executeInitializeFunction`, `executePostProcessing`, the
+  rotations) automatically switch to the batch functions, without copying
+  any data;
+- each batch function also takes an execution policy
+  (`mgis::BatchExecutionPolicy`), which selects the queue of the
+  computations;
+- the location of the arrays (`mgis::MemoryLocation`: host, device or
+  shared memory) is declared by the calling code and checked against the
+  memory space of the library. The functions working on the host refuse
+  arrays located on a device;
+- a material data manager can allocate its arrays with a memory resource
+  given by its initializer. Memory resources for the managed memory of
+  `CUDA` and `HIP`, the shared memory of `SYCL` and `Kokkos` are provided
+  as headers (`MGIS/MemoryResources`);
+- the `evaluate` function evaluates a material property on a set of
+  points, as a batch for a `generic-parallel` material property, point by
+  point otherwise;
+- the functions acting on a single point report an error for a
+  `generic-parallel` library instead of calling a null pointer.
+
